/-!
# Relational composition of tuple correspondence germs

A finite correspondence between the loci of two coordinate tuples is presented at a generic
point by a pair of tuples `(x, y)`, with `x` of rank one over `k` and each coordinate of either
tuple algebraic over the field generated by the other: these are the clauses of blueprint (8.1).
Its germ is the vanishing ideal `I(x, y)` together with the existence of such a presentation
(`TupleCorrespondenceGerm`). Composition is relational (`TupleCorrespondenceGerm.Composes`): a
germ `E` is a composite of `C` and `D` if some presentations `(x, y)` of `C` and `(y, z)` of `D`
share their middle tuple literally and `E` is the germ of `(x, z)`. No composite is selected.

The index types of the four tuples lie in independent universes. In an algebraically closed
ambient field, for finite index types:

* `TupleCorrespondenceGerm.composes_assoc`: relational composition is associative, meaning both
  parenthesizations have the same possible final germs;
* `TupleCorrespondenceGerm.exists_composes_of_middle_ideal_eq`: two germs whose middle loci agree
  have a composite;
* `TupleCorrespondenceGerm.composes_ofPair_carriers_eq`: the ideals of the composites of the
  germs of `(x, y)` and `(y, z)` are exactly the contractions to the endpoint variables `X, Z` of
  the vanishing ideals of the irreducible components of
  `Spec (k[X, Y, Z] ⧸ (I(x, y) + I(y, z)))` with dense image in `Spec (k[Y] ⧸ I(y))`. This is the
  source's composition by components of `C ×_W D`; a composite germ is the locus of the endpoint
  image of such a component, which can be smaller than the component itself;
* `TupleCorrespondenceGerm.composes_threefold_carriers_eq`: with both middle tuples fixed, the
  final germs of either parenthesization of a threefold composite are exactly the loci of the
  endpoint pairs `(x', w')` for which `(x', y)` has the locus of `(x, y)` and `(z, w')` has the
  locus of `(z, w)`. `ThreefoldIncidence` identifies them with the components of the threefold
  fiber product.

Both presentations are aligned by ambient automorphisms extending equalities of loci
(`exists_ambientAutomorphism_of_idealOf_eq`), and the components are identified by
`locusIncidence_dominatingComponents_eq_jointLoci`.

This is the tuple germ layer of the geometric fiber-product bridge of blueprint §8.1 (#5).
`TupleCompositionField` derives target rank one and proves the generated joint-field inclusion
and finite-extension clauses.

`LocusComponentField` identifies each actual middle-dominating component's coordinate ring and
fraction field with the realized joint generated ring and compositum, including polynomial
representative formulas. The remaining source obligations are recorded in the book's hard-kernel
chapter and the current frontier of `PROJECT_GOAL.md`.

This module is part of the formalization of the Evans–Hrushovski–Gismatullin
reconstruction theorem; the source of truth is `sources/blueprint.tex`.

**Status:** proved (#5, C2 support).
-/


